.SH NAME
choom \- Minimal SSH terminal\-sharing relay
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBchoom\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Minimal SSH terminal\-sharing relay
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
choom\-server(1)
Run the central relay
.TP
choom\-host(1)
Share your local shell through a relay
.TP
choom\-view(1)
Attach to a shared session as a viewer (a convenience wrapper over `ssh`)
.TP
choom\-clients(1)
List the viewers of your session
.TP
choom\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  Share your shell on a relay:
      choom host \-s relay.example.com
  Run a relay with the web view:
      choom server \-H relay.example.com \-w 0.0.0.0:8080
  List who is watching your session:
      choom clients

Viewers need no choom binary — they attach with stock ssh:
      ssh <token>@relay.example.com
